{
	"title": "Factoriser un trinôme à l'aide de ses racines",
	"description": "Forme factorisée a(x − x₁)(x − x₂)",
	"grades": ["1_SPE"],
	"theme": "Fonctions",
	"domain": "Polynôme du second degré",
	"status": "draft",
	"subdomain": "Formes",
	"level": 3,
	"delay": 90,
	"variations": [
		{
			"statement": "Le polynôme $P(x)={{eval:ax^2+bx+c}}$ a pour racines ${{r}}$ et ${{s}}$. Écris-le sous forme factorisée.\n\n$P(x)=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "x",
					"expression": "x|x"
				},
				{
					"name": "a",
					"expression": "1..3;±"
				},
				{
					"name": "r",
					"expression": "1..6;±"
				},
				{
					"name": "s",
					"expression": "1..6;±"
				},
				{
					"name": "b",
					"expression": "eval:-a*(r+s)"
				},
				{
					"name": "c",
					"expression": "eval:a*r*s"
				}
			],
			"conditions": ["r < s && r != -s"],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:a*(x-r)*(x-s)}}",
					"requiredForm": {
						"pattern": "u*($x+v)*($x+w)"
					}
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"Un polynôme du second degré de racines $x_1$ et $x_2$ s'écrit $a(x-x_1)(x-x_2)$. Ici $a={{a}}$, $x_1={{r}}$ et $x_2={{s}}$, donc $P(x)={{eval:a*(x-r)*(x-s)}}$."
				]
			}
		},
		{
			"statement": "Factorise le polynôme $P(x)={{eval:ax^2+bx+c}}$ en calculant d'abord ses racines.\n\n$P(x)=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "x",
					"expression": "x|x"
				},
				{
					"name": "a",
					"expression": "1..2;±"
				},
				{
					"name": "r",
					"expression": "1..5;±"
				},
				{
					"name": "s",
					"expression": "1..5;±"
				},
				{
					"name": "b",
					"expression": "eval:-a*(r+s)"
				},
				{
					"name": "c",
					"expression": "eval:a*r*s"
				}
			],
			"conditions": ["r < s && r != -s"],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:a*(x-r)*(x-s)}}",
					"requiredForm": {
						"pattern": "u*($x+v)*($x+w)"
					}
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"On calcule le discriminant avec $a={{a}}$, $b={{b}}$ et $c={{c}}$ : $\\Delta={{eval:b;()}}^2-4\\times{{eval:a;()}}\\times{{eval:c;()}}={{eval:b^2-4*a*c}}>0$, et $\\sqrt{\\Delta}={{eval:sqrt(b^2-4*a*c)}}$.",
					"$$x_1=\\dfrac{ {{eval:-b}}-{{eval:sqrt(b^2-4*a*c)}} }{ {{eval:2*a}} }={{eval:(-b-sqrt(b^2-4*a*c))/(2*a)}} \\qquad x_2=\\dfrac{ {{eval:-b}}+{{eval:sqrt(b^2-4*a*c)}} }{ {{eval:2*a}} }={{eval:(-b+sqrt(b^2-4*a*c))/(2*a)}}$$",
					"Un polynôme du second degré de racines $x_1$ et $x_2$ s'écrit $a(x-x_1)(x-x_2)$, donc $P(x)={{eval:a*(x-r)*(x-s)}}$."
				]
			}
		},
		{
			"statement": "Le polynôme $P(x)={{eval:ax^2+bx+c}}$ a pour racines ${{r}}$ et ${{eval:q/a}}$. Écris-le sous la forme $a(x-x_1)(x-x_2)$.\n\n$P(x)=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "x",
					"expression": "x|x"
				},
				{
					"name": "a",
					"expression": "2|3"
				},
				{
					"name": "r",
					"expression": "1..4;±"
				},
				{
					"name": "q",
					"expression": "1..5;±"
				},
				{
					"name": "s",
					"expression": "eval:q/a"
				},
				{
					"name": "b",
					"expression": "eval:-(a*r+q)"
				},
				{
					"name": "c",
					"expression": "eval:q*r"
				}
			],
			"conditions": ["mod(q,a) != 0"],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{a}}(x{{eval:-r;+}})(x{{eval:-q/a;+}})",
					"requiredForm": {
						"pattern": "u*($x+v)*($x+w)"
					}
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"Un polynôme du second degré de racines $x_1$ et $x_2$ s'écrit $a(x-x_1)(x-x_2)$. Ici $a={{a}}$, $x_1={{r}}$ et $x_2={{eval:q/a}}$.",
					"Donc $P(x)={{a}}(x{{eval:-r;+}})(x{{eval:-q/a;+}})$."
				]
			}
		}
	],
